From 13e5e2aff2785dbd36dbd936d65dc8859c0fcfc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:25:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: piano_mca: apply the factory high-load thermal
 policy

Read both original battery temperatures and four board thermistors through
IIO. Preserve the factory calibration units and high-load trigger/clear
levels, constrain the total battery budget and the voltage-specific buck
FCC, and expose the computed skin temperature through the thermal API.

Retire the pump before tightening current. Missing sensors stop charging
while retaining input and ordinary float-voltage control; successful reads
restore only this limit and retain its hysteresis. Cache the reported
computed temperature for a bounded time, and stop polling before releasing
its providers. Keep manual, full, hardware-fault and user cooling limits
independent. No userspace charging state machine or FFC path is added.

Enable the board's native ADC and original-temperature provider. Match
PMIH010x's documented 18-pin GPIO layout so the existing thermistor pinctrl
states use the standard driver rather than deferring ADC setup forever.

Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
---
